&lt;p&gt;Former Program Director, NCI/NIH&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Title: Curating and Administering a Portfolio at the Intersection of Iron and Cancer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abstract:&amp;nbsp;As the role of iron metabolism in cancer progression and therapy gains prominence, establishing a cohesive research landscape requires a blend of scientific insight and administrative experience. Drawing on my experience as Program Director, this presentation provides a dual-perspective look at building a high-impact research portfolio from the ground up. I will first detail the strategic development of the &amp;quot;Iron and Cancer&amp;quot; portfolio, highlighting how emerging trends like ferroptosis and dysregulation of iron metabolism in cancer were identified and prioritized. The discussion will then shift to the mechanics of program administration. I will outline the lifecycle of grants, portfolio management&amp;mdash;from initial curation and funding oversight to the long-term stewardship of funded projects. Attendees will gain a transparent understanding of how programmatic leadership transforms a niche scientific interest into a robust, sustainable research program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Host: Brent Stockwell&lt;/p&gt;

